WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.137
Drivers are how the platform
reaches the outside world.

2
00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:08.938
CA drivers request certificates
from AD CS, public CAs or AWS.

3
00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:13.125
Application drivers install
certificates on IIS, F5,

4
00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:17.788
NetScaler, Key Vault and the
rest, usually without any agent.

5
00:00:17.788 --> 00:00:19.324
Where a driver can't reach,

6
00:00:19.324 --> 00:00:22.688
a small Server Agent checks
in and does the work locally.

7
00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.809
Everything is stored in
one SQL Server database,

8
00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:29.007
and that database's secrets
are protected by a key —

9
00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:33.376
either a software key you must back
up, or a hardware security module.

10
00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:38.020
Lose that key and you lose the data,
which is why it's treated as Tier 0.
